WEBVTT

00:49:29.108 --> 00:49:31.083
DB: I think it is for 90% of the people,

00:49:31.107 --> 00:49:33.176
but there are 10%
of the mockers out there.

00:49:33.200 --> 00:49:37.461
And I've found that when my columns
have generated the most vicious response,

00:49:37.485 --> 00:49:39.534
it's because I admitted
some vulnerability,

00:49:39.558 --> 00:49:40.883
something I did wrong.

00:49:40.907 --> 00:49:45.469
And there's something about vulnerability
that once, gets a lot of people to say,

00:49:45.493 --> 00:49:48.810
"OK, you're a real human being,
you're not just some pundit blowhard,"

00:49:48.834 --> 00:49:52.491
but there's another group
that vulnerability enrages them,

00:49:52.515 --> 00:49:54.730
and they see it as a chance to pounce.

00:49:54.754 --> 00:50:00.097
And so, the courage to be vulnerable
is one of the key courages of our time.